\import{fnip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fnip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Two numbers at one instant}
\date{2026-11-25}

\p{At one instant the Morris–Lecar model assigns a pair
#{(V,n)}
\citet{§3.2, equations (3.1), pp. 49–50}{ermentrout2010mathematical}.
#{V} is the membrane potential. #{n} is the potassium variable in
those equations. The pair is a point of the plane. A voltage recording
keeps #{V} and omits #{n}.}

\p{One value of #{V} is shared by many pairs. A rule is still required
to send an initial pair to the pair at a later time. Which identities
does that rule have to satisfy?}
